From: Opsero Electronic Design Inc. <support@opsero.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: axienet: HSE link poll must double-read latched status

The HSE RX status register (l_ethernet STAT_RX_STATUS_REG1 / CMAC
STAT_RX_STATUS) is latched-low and cleared on read. The link poll read
it once per cycle, so it always saw the history of the interval - which,
while the link was down, always included the poll's own GT reset pulse
from the previous cycle. The result is a self-defeating loop: the GT
aligns within the poll period, the poll reads the latched pre-alignment
low, declares the link down and resets the GT again. The link never
comes up on an idle system; on the bench it only came up when external
register reads (devmem debugging) flushed the latch mid-interval.

Read the status register twice: the first read flushes the latch, the
second returns the current state. Verified on zcu106_hpc0 hardware
(2x QSFP28 FMC, 40GBASE-R4, passive loopback plugs): with the flush in
place both ports align and carrier comes up on the next poll cycle.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
@@ -1091,10 +1091,21 @@
 						hse_link_work.work);
 	struct net_device *ndev = lp->ndev;
 	bool link_up;
-	u32 val;
+	u32 off, val;
 
-	val = axienet_ior(lp, lp->hse_leth ? HSE_LETH_STAT_RX_STATUS_OFFSET
-					   : HSE_CMAC_STAT_RX_STATUS_OFFSET);
+	off = lp->hse_leth ? HSE_LETH_STAT_RX_STATUS_OFFSET
+			   : HSE_CMAC_STAT_RX_STATUS_OFFSET;
+
+	/* The RX status bits are latched-low, cleared on read: one read
+	 * returns the history since the previous read, which - while the
+	 * link is down - always includes our own GT reset from the last
+	 * poll cycle, so a single read shows the link down forever even
+	 * once alignment has completed (reset -> align -> read the
+	 * pre-alignment low -> reset again). Read twice: the first read
+	 * flushes the latch, the second samples the current state.
+	 */
+	axienet_ior(lp, off);
+	val = axienet_ior(lp, off);
 	link_up = (val & HSE_RX_STATUS_MASK) && (val & HSE_RX_ALIGNED_MASK);
 
 	if (link_up && !netif_carrier_ok(ndev)) {
